#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "How is Okular Sustainable?"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "Eco"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "Eco-Certification"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "eco-certification-icon.svg"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"Blue Angel certified for transparency in energy use, a longer hardware "
"operating life, and user freedoms.\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "Energy Efficiency"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "energy-efficiency-icon.svg"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"Software efficiency determines the energy demands and operating life of "
"digital infrastructure.\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "Transparency & Autonomy"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "user-autonomy-icon.svg"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"A Free Software license makes for the efficient, long-term, and sustainable "
"use of hardware.\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "Ethics & Privacy"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "ethics-and-privacy-icon.svg"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"The [four freedoms](https://fsfe.org/freesoftware/index.en.html) are "
"critical for an inclusive, equitable, and ecologically sustainable "
"digitization.\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"Medal by Ongycon, Green Lamp by Stefania Servidio, User by Guru, Ethics by\n"
"Ruben Hojo from [Noun Project](https://thenounproject.com/) (CC BY 3.0)\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"Okular is proud to be the first computer software worldwide to have\n"
"received the Blue Angel seal in 2022. Introduced in 1978, the Blue Angel is\n"
"the first ever ecolabel worldwide and the official environmental label of\n"
"the German government. In 2020, the German Environment Agency\n"
"(Umweltbundesamt) released the award criteria for desktop software with\n"
"three main categories: (A) Resource & Energy Efficiency, (B) Potential\n"
"Hardware Operating Life, and (C) User Autonomy. Software products that\n"
"demonstrate compliance with these criteria enable longer and more efficient\n"
"use of hardware.\n"
"\n"
"Interested to know more? Check out the KDE Eco handbook [\"Applying The "
"Blue\n"
"Angel Criteria To Free Software\"](https://eco.kde.org/handbook/).\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"Download the most recent reports for Okular's [Idle Mode](https://okular.kde."
"org/eco/okular_energy-consumption-report_idle.pdf) and [Standard Usage "
"Scenario](https://okular.kde.org/eco/okular_energy-consumption-report_SUS."
"pdf) energy consumption measurements.\n"
"Software design and implementation have a significant impact on the energy\n"
"consumption of the systems it is a part of. By becoming aware of how\n"
"software affects energy consumption and providing tools to quantify them,\n"
"it is possible to drive down energy consumption and increase efficiency.\n"
"This contributes to a more sustainable use of energy as one of the shared\n"
"resources of our planet.\n"
"\n"
"Learn more about KDE's work on energy efficiency and sustainable software\n"
"at the [KDE Eco](https://eco.kde.org/) website.\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"KDE wants to [put you in the driver's seat](https://community.kde.org/KDE/"
"Vision) with all of its software, including Okular. Okular is available "
"under a [Free Software license](https://invent.kde.org/graphics/okular/-/"
"blob/master/COPYING), and the source code is readily available at [Okular's "
"repository](https://invent.kde.org/graphics/okular). With Okular's [data "
"format documentation](https://okular.kde.org/formats), you will never again "
"be subject to vendor lock in from proprietary formats. Moreover, enhancing "
"Okular's functionality is possible with its [API Documentation](https://api."
"kde.org/okular/html/index.html). [Install and uninstall instructions]"
"(https://userbase.kde.org/Tutorials/Install_KDE_software) are available to "
"make sure users are not burdened by unwanted software components on their "
"machines. And for those who want long-term support for their favorite "
"software, Okular's [full list of release announcements](https://okular.kde."
"org/news/) ǵoes all the way back to 2006 and will continue well into the "
"future.\n"
"\n"
"By guaranteeing transparency and autonomy, developers and users can ensure\n"
"that their software reduces environmental harm in more ways than one,\n"
"whether by keeping devices in use for longer, or by reducing the software’s\n"
"use of energy and resources while in use.\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"Being Free & Open Source Software, Okular's source code is available for\n"
"all to use, study, share, improve, and most of all, enjoy. KDE software\n"
"will always be available to all without being restricted to materially,\n"
"educationally, or socially privileged people. [KDE's Code of\n"
"Conduct](https://kde.org/code-of-conduct/) provides guidelines to support\n"
"everyone in the community for a positive and inspiring atmosphere. This is\n"
"necessary for software development that meets all its users' needs,\n"
"wherever they are, on whatever device they own -- and not just ones vendors\n"
"want to sell.\n"
"\n"
"KDE [envisions](https://community.kde.org/KDE/Vision) a \"world in which\n"
"everyone has control over their digital life and enjoys freedom and\n"
"privacy.\" Freedom from unethical practices such as unwanted data "
"collection\n"
"and tracking or [psychological\n"
"targeting](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facebook"
"%E2%80%93Cambridge_Analytica_data_scandal)\n"
"is not only good for society, but it also reduces the carbon footprint of\n"
"digital technology. A default opt out for ads and telemetry decreases\n"
"energy demands on both end-user devices and servers running the ads or\n"
"mining the data, and it reduces the energy needed for network traffic.\n"
"[KDE's Privacy Policy](https://kde.org/privacypolicy-apps/) ensures that\n"
"its software does not collect any information from users except when users\n"
"actively and explicitly opt in to it!\n"
"\n"
"KDE is [software for you](https://kde.org/for/), by you!\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "Want to learn more about sustainable software?"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"KDE has the [goal](https://community.kde.org/Goals/Sustainable_Software) of "
"providing software that reduces software's environmental impact. Let's make "
"energy efficient software and digital sustainability part of the Free "
"Software community. We can live up to our responsibility for this and future "
"generations!\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "Okular's Path Toward Sustainability"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"In 2022 Okular was the awarded the [Blue Angel ecolabel for sustainable\n"
"software\n"
"design](https://www.blauer-engel.de/en/productworld/resources-and-energy-"
"efficient-software-products),\n"
"becoming the first eco-certified computer program within the Global\n"
"Ecolabelling Network.\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid "Okular was awarded the Blue Angel ecolabel in 2022."
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"With KDE’s long-standing [mission](https://community.kde.org/KDE/Mission)\n"
"and guiding [vision](https://community.kde.org/KDE/Vision) since its\n"
"founding in 1996, as well as the talent and capabilities of its community\n"
"members, KDE is a pioneer in championing sustainable software. In 2021 KDE\n"
"started [KDE Eco](https://eco.kde.org/), a project with the goal of putting\n"
"KDE and Free Software at the forefront of sustainable software engineering,\n"
"and in 2022 the KDE community voted to have [Sustainable\n"
"Software](https://community.kde.org/Goals/Sustainable_Software) as one of\n"
"its overarching goals.\n"
"\n"
"Sustainability is not new for Free & Open Source Software (FOSS)&mdash;the\n"
"[four freedoms](https://fsfe.org/freesoftware/index.en.html) have always\n"
"made [Free Software sustainable\n"
"software](https://fsfe.org/freesoftware/sustainability/). But now, the two\n"
"pillars of FOSS&mdash;transparency and user autonomy&mdash;have wider\n"
"recognition for their impacts on sustainability, and were incorporated into\n"
"the sustainability criteria set by the German Environment Agency through\n"
"the Blue Angel ecolabel.\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:0
msgid ""
"<em>Many people don't realize that software can contribute to hardware "
"having\n"
"to be decommissioned, thus wasting resources unnecessarily.</em>"
msgstr ""

#: content/eco.md:152
msgid ""
"Free & Open Source Software guarantees transparency and hands control over "
"to users, rather than obligating them to work with certain vendors or "
"service providers. This allows users to decide what they want from the "
"software they use and, in turn, make decisions about the hardware they use "
"as well. Users are able to reduce the energy consumption of their programs "
"with little or no loss in functionality, installing only what they need, no "
"more and no less; they can also avoid invasive advertising or data-mining "
"options which run processes in the background, further consuming resources "
"on the device and in the network. As for FOSS developers, they typically "
"continue to support hardware that the industry would be eager to make "
"obsolete, providing users with up-to-date and secure software for devices "
"that might otherwise be discarded as e-waste and end up polluting landfills."
msgstr ""

